INT. 24-HOUR LAUNDROMAT - NIGHT

Fluorescent hum. A row of dryers turning. Orange plastic chairs bolted to the floor.

A GIRL, 20s, hoodie, headphones, sits on top of a washing machine with a paperback. She doesn't look up.

A TALL MAN, 30s, rumpled, enters with a pillowcase of clothes. He scans the machines. Only one is free: the one under her.

TALL MAN
Is that one taken?

GIRL
You're welcome to it.

TALL MAN
You're sitting on it.

GIRL
It's running.

He studies the machine. It vibrates under her.

TALL MAN
Is it?

GIRL
Spin cycle.

He leans on the dryer next to her. She turns a page.

TALL MAN
Good book?

GIRL
It's okay.

TALL MAN
What's it about?

GIRL
A man who talks to strangers in laundromats.

He laughs. She almost smiles.

TALL MAN
I'm Felix.

GIRL
Wynonona. Wynona.

FELIX
Which?

WYNONA
The second one.

FELIX
Nice to meet you, Wynona.

She closes the book. Slides off the machine. It shudders to a halt.

WYNONA
All yours.

FELIX
Thanks.

He empties the pillowcase into the drum. A single sock falls to the floor. She hands it back.
